.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# data/snapshots is a symlink to ~/Library/Application Support/apex-fpl/snapshots
# (kept outside ~/Documents due to macOS TCC restrictions on launchd — see
# docs/fpl_gap_analysis.md and research/research_plan.md). The symlink itself
# is fine to track; the actual snapshot payloads are not source and are large.
data/snapshots/**
data/logs/
data/canonical/
artifacts/

# data/raw/ (Phase 13 pipeline captures, data/raw/gw{n}/*.json) is
# deliberately NOT ignored -- CLAUDE.md documents it as a committed,
# immutable raw-capture tier alongside the prediction/result ledgers,
# and every prediction's data_sources[].sha256 only means anything if
# the file it points at is actually in the repo. It had been caught by
# this blanket rule since before Phase 13 existed; ~360KB/file, small
# enough that committing it forever is not a real storage concern.

# The 4 seasons scripts/run_production_recommendation.py's
# COLD_START_MINUTES_TRAIN_SEASONS and apex_fpl.serving.live_data's
# TEAM_MODEL_FALLBACK_SEASONS name are carved out of the data/external/
# blanket ignore WHOLE (every file present locally for that season), not
# file-by-file. File-by-file was tried first and broke: several
# PRE-EXISTING Part A tests (test_ownership.py,
# test_replay_manager_position_filter.py, test_scenario_builder.py)
# gate on "does this season's data look present" with their own
# `_data_available()`-style checks, keyed on merged_gw.csv/fixtures.csv
# as a proxy for "the whole season is there" -- a proxy that was true
# before this carve-out existed, and silently false once only SOME of a
# season's files were committed, so those tests stopped skipping and
# hard-failed on a DIFFERENT missing file instead. Committing each named
# season in full (not just the specific file the live model reads)
# keeps that "present means present" assumption true, at low cost: 3-6MB
# per season, all of it CSV.
#
# All 3 live-workflow crashes this fixed, in order: fixtures.csv +
# teams.csv missing for the team-model fallback (TEAM_MODEL_FALLBACK_
# SEASONS); merged_gw.csv missing for the cold-start minutes model
# (COLD_START_MINUTES_TRAIN_SEASONS); teams.csv/players_raw.csv missing
# for the pre-existing tests above once merged_gw.csv alone existed.
# data/canonical/ was checked and does NOT need the same treatment --
# silver.run_build() (which predict.py always calls first) writes it
# fresh from real live data on every run. See CLAUDE.md.
data/external/*
!data/external/vaastav/
data/external/vaastav/*
!data/external/vaastav/2020-21/
!data/external/vaastav/2022-23/
!data/external/vaastav/2023-24/
!data/external/vaastav/2024-25/
